  "note": "Two harmony lines over the 1st, 5th, 6th and 4th chords: each line rung note by note on the staff by its `line` (so the text no longer spells it out), then either line with short runs joining its notes. The chords are tokens counted the long way, and the block moves to any key and from 76 to 92 bpm, with the line about another key marked {{?key}}.",
  "exercise": {
    "title": "Two harmony lines, then runs between",
    "area": "voice",
    "tags": [
      "sing",
      "improv"
    ],
    "topic": "voice-harmony",
    "concepts": [
      "harmony-line"
    ],
    "why": "A harmony line moves as little as it can from one chord note to the next, so it is easy to hold and leaves room to decorate.",
    "learnBefore": [
      "/course/6/harmony-line",
      "/course/9/improvising-a-melody"
    ],
    "cells": [
      {
        "type": "section",
        "heading": "The lower line",
        "minutes": 3,
        "cells": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Press Start exercise below: the mic and the backing track start together, at {{=bpm}}. The backing track plays {{chord:I}}, {{chord:V}}, {{chord:vi}} and {{chord:IV}}, one bar each.\n{{chord:I}} is the 1st chord of the key, built on {{1}}, {{chord:V}} is the 5th, built on {{5}}, {{chord:vi}} is the 6th, built on {{6}}, and {{chord:IV}} is the 4th, built on {{4}}. Sing the ringed note over each chord, one long note per bar. Sing it on \"oo\".\nPractice until each new note arrives with its chord."
          },
          {
            "type": "tool",
            "tool": {
              "type": "staff",
              "scale": "major-ionian",
              "key": "g",
              "voice": "baritone",
              "notes": [
                "1",
                "2",
                "3",
                "4",
                "5",
                "6"
              ],
              "labels": "degree",
              "line": [
                "3",
                "2",
                "1",
                "1"
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "tool",
            "tool": {
              "type": "backing-track",
              "progression": "pop",
              "key": "g",
              "style": "ballad",
              "parts": {
                "drums": "on",
                "bass": "off",
                "keys": "always"
              },
              "bpm": 76
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "section",
        "heading": "The upper line",
        "minutes": 3,
        "cells": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Press Start exercise below: the mic and the backing track start together. Now the line above it: sing the ringed note over each chord. Sing it on \"ee\".\nPractice until you can start either line without looking at the staff.\n{{?key}}In another key the notes are new, but each line still moves by a step or stays put."
          },
          {
            "type": "tool",
            "tool": {
              "type": "staff",
              "scale": "major-ionian",
              "key": "g",
              "voice": "baritone",
              "notes": [
                "1",
                "2",
                "3",
                "4",
                "5",
                "6"
              ],
              "labels": "degree",
              "line": [
                "5",
                "5",
                "6",
                "6"
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "tool",
            "tool": {
              "type": "backing-track",
              "progression": "pop",
              "key": "g",
              "style": "ballad",
              "parts": {
                "drums": "on",
                "bass": "off",
                "keys": "always"
              },
              "bpm": 76
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "section",
        "heading": "Runs between the notes",
        "minutes": 4,
        "cells": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Press Start exercise below: the mic and the backing track start together. Sing either line, and in the last beat of a bar join its note to the next with a short run of steps, or put a turn on a held note. Sing the long notes on \"oo\" and the runs on \"ah\".\nIf a run makes you late, hold the next note plain and try again a bar later."
          },
          {
